course: dictionary
lesson: 1572
title: Chariot in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A chariot is a two-wheeled cart pulled by horses. You will meet the word in history lessons about Romans, Egyptians and Celts like Boudicca, and in Bible stories and myths. The words around it give you clues: «The Circus Maximus held perhaps 150,000 fans, who cheered for chariot teams.» Fans cheering for teams tells you chariots were raced, not just parked in a yard.
explain: The clues can also tell you what chariots were for. «An early form of chess called chaturanga was played in India about 1,500 years ago, with pieces like elephants, chariots and foot soldiers.» Elephants, chariots and soldiers all belong to an army, so chariots were part of ancient fighting. A dictionary says the same thing: chariots were used in war and racing.
explain: Some words have a second meaning. In a poem or a story, chariot can mean any grand carriage, like a golden coach. The famous song «Swing Low, Sweet Chariot» uses the word in its own special way. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A chariot is a two-wheeled cart pulled by horses.
fact: «Chariot races» were part of the Olympic Games, which began in 776 BC at Olympia.
fact: «Chariot teams» at the Circus Maximus were called the Reds, Whites, Greens and Blues.
fact: «The First Emperor» was buried with clay chariots, horses and soldiers, the Terracotta Army.
fact: In literary writing, chariot can mean any grand carriage.
exercise: What is a chariot? | A large boat with sails | A tall tower of stone | A hat worn by soldiers | *A two-wheeled cart pulled by horses
exercise: «Crowds cheered chariot teams at the Circus Maximus, like football fans.» What did the crowds cheer for? | Singing in a choir | *Chariot teams in races | Chariot racing | Ice skating
exercise: A poet writes, «She rode in a golden chariot to the palace ball.» What does chariot mean here? | A small bird | *Any grand carriage | Ice cream van | A kind of sword
test: «The First Emperor was buried with about 8,000 life-size clay soldiers, horses and chariots.» What were the chariots made of? | Stone | *Clay | Gold | Wood
test: Which phrase shows a chariot used in battle? | Chariot teams | *War chariot | Chariot race | Swing Low, Sweet Chariot
exam: From «pieces like elephants, chariots and foot soldiers», what do the clues suggest about chariots? | Modern cars and trains | *Ancient armies and battles | Ocean fish and boats | Farm tools and animals
